// THE G-BUFFER'S SURFACE CLASS (PHOTON-2 stage 2d): the prepass writes the normals target
// (R10G10B10A2, OgreChain.cpp) with its two-bit alpha at 1 - upstream's constant. FOLIAGE
// - an ALPHA-TESTED (cut-out) surface, and only that (PHOTON-2 K5: a double-sided OPAQUE
// material is not foliage; the cull is no class, and UE derives its foliage class from the
// shading model, not from culling) - writes 0 there instead, so the screen-probe gather's
// pixel history (rq_probe_integrate.comp, jah_probe_history.glsl) can hold a foliage pixel
// to its own looser depth test and never blend it with a non-foliage history. The hook runs
// after the body has written the target. Atom's decode carries the class in its own
// property atom_cutout (the bucket's members are alpha-tested; its twin tests nothing, the
// id pass masked the coverage). DISJOINT from every other definition
// of this hook: the gather's blended-prepass discard (alpha blend), the card capture's (its
// own property), the fog's and the photon view's (not the prepass), the hit decode's (its own
// property). A depth-only prepass writes no normals target.
@property( hlms_prepass && !hlms_alphablend && !hlms_shadowcaster && !hlms_render_depth_only && !jah_card_capture && !atom_hit_mode )
@property( alpha_test || atom_cutout )
@piece( custom_ps_posExecution )
	outPs_normals.w = _h( 0.0 );
@end
@end
@end
